{
  "title": "Scholarship Application Overview",
  "subtitle": "Summary of applicant demographics, financial status, and processing outcomes",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Applications",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_apps FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Approved Rate",
      "sql": "SELECT (COUNT(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Approved' THEN 1 END) * 100.0) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS approval_rate FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": "%"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Family Income",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(\"Family Income\") AS avg_income FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": "INR"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Applications by Status",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Status\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Status",
      "y": ["count"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Applications by Category",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Category\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Category",
      "y": ["count"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top Schemes by Volume",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Name of scheme\", COUNT(*) AS total_apps, AVG(\"Marks %\") AS avg_marks FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The board has received a total of {{p1}} scholarship applications. The current approval rate stands at {{p2}}%, indicating the proportion of applicants who have successfully cleared the initial review stages.\n\nFinancially, the average family income among applicants is {{p3}}. This metric helps in assessing the economic profile of the beneficiary pool and ensuring that funds are directed to those with the greatest need.\n\nIn terms of demographic distribution, the most common applicant category is {{p5[0].Category}} with {{p5[0].count}} applications. The status breakdown shows that {{p4[0].Status}} is the most frequent outcome, accounting for {{p4[0].count}} cases.\n\nThe most popular scheme is {{p6[0].Name of scheme}}, which has attracted {{p6[0].total_apps}} applications. Applicants for this scheme have an average mark percentage of {{p6[0].avg_marks}}."
}

{
  "title": "Scholarship Scheme Progress by District",
  "subtitle": "Overview of application status, scheme distribution, and pending cases across districts",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Applications",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS total FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Pending Cases",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS pending FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Approved & Disbursed",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS completed FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" IN ('Approved', 'Disbursed')",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "stacked_bar",
      "title": "Application Status by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\" AS district, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Approved' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS approved, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Disbursed' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS disbursed, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Pending' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS pending, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Rejected' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS rejected, SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Under Review' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS under_review FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
      "x": "district",
      "y": ["approved", "disbursed", "pending", "rejected", "under_review"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Pending Cases by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\" AS district, COUNT(*) AS pending_count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "district",
      "y": ["pending_count"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Pending Applications by Scheme and District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Name of scheme\" AS scheme, \"District\" AS district, COUNT(*) AS pending_count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending' GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 3 DESC LIMIT 20"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard tracks scholarship application progress across districts, highlighting total volume, completed cases, and pending items. The total number of applications is {{p1}}, with {{p2}} currently pending and {{p3}} already approved or disbursed.\n\nThe stacked bar chart shows the status breakdown by district, allowing quick identification of areas with high pending or rejected counts. The bar chart isolates pending cases by district, with the highest pending count in {{p5}}.\n\nThe table lists the top pending applications by scheme and district, with the most common pending scheme-district combination being {{p6}}."
}

{
  "title": "Child Fitness Improvement Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Tracking physical performance changes from baseline to endline by location and coach",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Children Tracked",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM \"baseline\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Improvement (sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "sec"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "reps"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Improvement by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Location\" AS location, AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
      "x": "location",
      "y": [
        "avg_improvement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement by Coach",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Coach\" AS coach, AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
      "x": "coach",
      "y": [
        "avg_improvement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "scatter",
      "title": "Shuttle Run vs Sit-ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Child name\" AS child, (b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS shuttle_improvement, (e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS situps_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "x": "shuttle_improvement",
      "y": [
        "situps_improvement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p7",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 10 Improvers (Shuttle Run)",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Child name\" AS child, b.\"Location\" AS location, b.\"Coach\" AS coach, b.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS baseline_shuttle, e.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS endline_shuttle, (b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" ORDER BY 6 DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard highlights the physical development of children across various locations and coaching groups. The total number of children tracked is {{p1}}, providing a baseline for the scope of the program.\n\nIn terms of speed, the average improvement in shuttle run time is {{p2}} seconds, indicating a general trend toward faster performance. The top performing location in terms of shuttle run improvement is {{p4}}, while the most effective coach for sit-ups is {{p5}}.\n\nThe scatter plot reveals the relationship between speed and strength improvements, with the top individual improver being {{p7}}. This data helps identify which coaching strategies and locations are yielding the best results."
}

{
  "title": "Fitness Programme Impact Summary",
  "subtitle": "Overview of participant progress and key performance indicators from baseline to endline.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Participants",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM \"baseline\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Improvement (sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "s"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Increase",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS increase FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "reps"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Shuttle Run Time by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Location\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_time FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 ASC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "location",
      "y": ["avg_time"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Sit-ups by Gender",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS avg_situps FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1",
      "x": "gender",
      "y": ["avg_situps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 10 Improvements in Shuttle Run",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Child name\", b.\"Location\", b.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS baseline_sec, e.\"Shuttle run sec\" AS endline_sec, (b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS improvement_sec FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL ORDER BY improvement_sec DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The fitness programme engaged {{p1}} children across various locations. The overall impact is reflected in the average shuttle run time reduction of {{p2}} seconds, indicating improved speed and agility.\n\nStrength training also showed positive results, with an average increase of {{p3}} sit-ups per child. This suggests enhanced core strength and endurance among the participants.\n\nGeographically, the top performing location for shuttle run times is {{p4}}, while gender-based analysis shows that {{p5}} achieved higher average sit-up counts. Individual success stories are highlighted in the table, where the top performer improved their shuttle run time by {{p6[0].improvement_sec}} seconds."
}

