{
  "title": "Gender Parity in Fitness Improvement",
  "subtitle": "Comparing baseline and endline performance metrics for boys and girls",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Participants",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"baseline\" UNION SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"endline\")",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Shuttle Run Time (sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_time FROM \"baseline\" GROUP BY 1 UNION ALL SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_time FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1",
      "x": "Gender",
      "y": ["avg_time"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Sit-ups",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS avg_situps FROM \"baseline\" GROUP BY 1 UNION ALL SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS avg_situps FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1",
      "x": "Gender",
      "y": ["avg_situps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Improvement by Gender",
      "sql": "WITH b AS (SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS base_shuttle, AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS base_situps FROM \"baseline\" GROUP BY 1), e AS (SELECT \"Gender\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS end_shuttle, AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS end_situps FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1) SELECT b.\"Gender\" AS gender, b.base_shuttle, e.end_shuttle, (b.base_shuttle - e.end_shuttle) AS shuttle_improvement, b.base_situps, e.end_situps, (e.end_situps - b.base_situps) AS situps_improvement FROM b JOIN e ON b.\"Gender\" = e.\"Gender\" ORDER BY 1"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This report examines whether boys and girls are improving at the same rate in physical fitness. We compare the average shuttle run times and sit-up counts from the baseline to the endline assessment.\n\nThe total number of participants tracked is {{p1}}. The bar charts show the average performance for each gender at both time points. A decrease in shuttle run time indicates improvement, while an increase in sit-ups indicates improvement.\n\nThe table below details the specific improvement metrics for each gender. The 'shuttle_improvement' column shows the reduction in time (positive is better), and 'situps_improvement' shows the increase in count (positive is better). By comparing these values, we can see if one gender is outpacing the other in specific areas."
}

